{% comment %}
  Desktop Homepage A/B Test (Variant B) — Top Sellers card, spec §4 module 5.
  DRAFT / NOT LAUNCHED.

  Parameters:
    product   - required, a Shopify product object from a block product picker
    slot      - required, 1-based position within the module (fss_hp_product_click prop)
    cta_label - optional, per-card CTA text

  Every displayed field is bound live to Shopify per Tim's Jul 29 item 7 —
  title, image, URL, price, availability, and condition. Nothing hardcoded, no
  Jul 26 concept snapshot values.

  Price follows the established theme convention, not the mobile branch's chain:
    - product.price                              -> current price
    - product.metafields.custom.retail_price     -> struck anchor
    - product.compare_at_price                   -> gates the Sale tag only
  See snippets/product-item.liquid:86-96 and
  sections/homepage-popular-fitness.liquid:86-93. compare_at_price_max is
  deliberately not used — it appears nowhere else in this theme.

  Condition badge reads product.metafields.custom.condition_state and handles
  the three states explicitly. A blank or unrecognised value renders NO badge
  rather than being inferred as New. Tim's launch-hold for such products is a
  process gate handled in QA, not here — this template only declines to guess.

  The value is downcased before testing, because the theme's own structured-data
  snippets test both 'as is' and 'As is' (snippets/schema-product.liquid:85,
  snippets/schema-collection.liquid:50) — matching a single casing risks a
  silent fallthrough to no badge. Test order is deliberate: 'remanufactured'
  before 'new', so a value merely containing "new" as a substring cannot
  mis-resolve a remanufactured product.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  comment
    downcase also coerces a nil metafield to an empty string, so every contains
    test below is simply false and the no-badge fallback holds.
  endcomment
  assign condition_state = product.metafields.custom.condition_state | downcase
  assign retail_price = product.metafields.custom.retail_price
  assign display_title = product.title | replace: '(Remanufactured)', '' | replace: '(New)', '' | replace: '(As Is)', '' | replace: '(As is)', '' | replace: '(as is)', '' | strip
-%}

<a
  class="fssd-top-sellers__card"
  href="{{ product.url }}"
  data-fss-hp-event="fss_hp_product_click"
  data-fss-hp-props='{"product_handle": {{ product.handle | json | escape }}, "slot": {{ slot }}}'
>
  <span class="fssd-top-sellers__media">
    {%- if product.featured_image != blank -%}
      <img
        src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 600 }}"
        srcset="
          {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 300 }} 300w,
          {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w
        "
        sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 30vw, (min-width: 750px) 45vw, 90vw"
        alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | default: display_title | escape }}"
        width="{{ product.featured_image.width }}"
        height="{{ product.featured_image.height }}"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      >
    {%- endif -%}

    <span class="fssd-top-sellers__tags">
      {%- if condition_state contains 'remanufactured' -%}
        <span class="condition-tag blue">{% render 'icon-remanufactured' %}Remanufactured</span>
      {%- elsif condition_state contains 'as is' -%}
        {%- comment -%} No icon snippet exists for As Is — text-only pill. {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="condition-tag neutral">As Is</span>
      {%- elsif condition_state contains 'new' -%}
        <span class="condition-tag">{% render 'icon-new' %}New</span>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if product.compare_at_price != blank -%}
        <span class="fssd-top-sellers__sale-tag">Sale</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>

    {%- unless product.available -%}
      <span class="fssd-top-sellers__soldout">
        {% render 'icon-sold-out' %}{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}
      </span>
    {%- endunless -%}
  </span>

  <span class="fssd-top-sellers__info">
    <span class="fssd-top-sellers__title">{{ display_title }}</span>

    <span class="fssd-top-sellers__prices">
      <span class="fssd-top-sellers__price">{{ product.price | money }}</span>
      {%- if retail_price != blank and retail_price > product.price -%}
        <span class="fssd-top-sellers__retail">{{ retail_price | money }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>

    {%- if cta_label != blank -%}
      <span class="fssd-top-sellers__cta">{{ cta_label }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </span>
</a>
